    "teach_4": {
      "id": "teach_4",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A tunnel follows exactly the same rule as a platform. The labels change; the geometry does not.\n\nA 100 m train entering a 500 m tunnel is not fully out until the front has travelled 600 m.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_4_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_4_step": {
      "id": "teach_4_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "At 108 km/hr = 30 m/s, 600 m takes 20 s.\n\nSo when the question says 'from the moment the front enters until the rear emerges', that phrase is telling you to add both lengths.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_4"
        }
      ]
    },
